WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.200
The good part about this topic is that the types of questions

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.460
you will see are very few and repetitive.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.000
One Category is that of forming numbers.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:18.080
We will be given a few digits, and will be asked to form numbers.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.560
For example, with these six digits we could be asked

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.380
of how many three-digit numbers we can form.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.080
Next, we might be asked to form anagrams.

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:33.180
Here, we will be given a word, a word like 'SILENT'.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.320
And asked for the number of anagrams

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.520
we can form with these six letters.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.540
An anagram of a word can be formed by simply rearranging its letters.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:46.480
An Anagram of 'SILENT' would be 'LISTEN'.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:51.880
Another anagram would be 'ESITLN'. And what does it mean?

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.440
Nothing, it's a meaningless anagram. It won't work in Scrubber.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.960
Another category of problems would be that of arranging people.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.280
We could be asked the number of ways,

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.140
in which we can see people on four chairs.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.420
Or maybe arrange them around a circular table.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:15.560
So in this session, and the next few, we will be looking at the first category.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.900
Arranging digits to form numbers.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:24.080
Let's say we have these five digits with us, and this is what we're asked!

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.080
Read the question well. How many

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:29.740
three digit numbers can be formed?

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:33.260
Let's form three slots here for the three digits.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.840
How many three-digit numbers can be form using these five digits?

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.640
And with this question, we have been given two conditions.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.420
First, it asks us the answer when repetition is not allowed.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.560
Let us understand the first condition!

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:53.380
Repetition is not allowed.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.480
Look at the number '1 1 1'.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.840
This is a three-digit number, but the digit 1 is repeated.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:04.940
Look at '2 3 2' or '5 4 4'.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:10.480
The digit 2 is repeated here. And the digit 4 is repeated here.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:12.760
By repetition not being allowed,

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:16.980
they mean that numbers like these should not be considered.

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:23.100
Each of the digits in the slot should be different. So numbers like 123,

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:28.280
341 or 524 are allowed as the digits in each case

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.900
are different from each other.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:34.140
So let's make 3 slots for the digits again.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.420
Now you can start thinking.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.920
How many three-digit numbers can be formed

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:41.900
if repetition is not allowed?

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:47.300
Before you think of the three-digit numbers, look at the slots individually.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.940
Let's look at the first slot or the hundreds place.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:54.280
In how many ways can you fill the first slot?

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.580
It is a simple question. You don't need to know

00:02:57.580 --> 00:03:00.320
permutations or combinations for this.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.760
In how many ways can you fill the first slot?

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.960
You can fill it with any of the five digits right?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.240
You can fill it with a 1 or a 2 or a 3 or a 4 or a 5.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.100
These are the five digits given to us.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:19.780
Did you listen carefully? I use the word or.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:23.080
1 or a 2 or a 3 and so on.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.700
So 5 ways and all .

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.120
We can fill it with any one of these five digits.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.240
Okay,

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.040
now listen to the next question carefully.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:35.780
Having filled the slot with one of the digits.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:38.660
In how many ways can we fill the second slot?

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:40.020
Easy!

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:45.160
We have used one of the digits here, it can be any digit doesn't matter.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:47.680
But after having used one,

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.640
four digits remain. So the second slot can be filled in four ways.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.960
If we fill the first slot with one.

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:59.360
We have two, three, four, five as possibilities here.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:02.180
If we fill the first slot with three

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:07.500
we have one, two ,four, five as the possibilities for the second slot.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.480
Now tell me having filled the first and the second slot

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:14.900
in how many ways can the third slot be filled?

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:22.660
It's simple.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:26.580
We have used up two digits here only three remain.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:29.920
The third slot can be filled in three ways.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:33.000
We're almost done. Almost.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.380
The first slot can be filled in five ways.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:40.260
The second and four ways and the third in three ways.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.180
So how many three-digit numbers

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.140
can be formed if repetition is not allowed?

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.840
Do we add these three or do we multiply them?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:50.420
What are we doing?

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:55.060
I'll be filling in the first slot or the second slot or the third slot?

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.180
Or are we filling in the first slot

00:04:57.340 --> 00:05:02.100
and the second slot and the third slot. It will be and.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:06.920
Yes, we are filling all three slots and not just one.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.780
And, as we have seen in the previous session is

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.520
multiplication.

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:14.060
So we multiply these three.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:19.240
Five times four is 20. And 20 times 3 is 60.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.120
There are 60 ways in which we can form three-digit numbers,

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.580
without repetition of digits.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:32.520
These include numbers like 123, 314 ,245 and so on.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.020
No repetition.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:36.820
Hope this was clear,

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:40.320
Here we started off with the hundredths place.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:43.220
Can we start off with the units place?

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.140
Of course yes, we could have.

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:48.820
If we would have started off with the units place,

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:52.840
we could say that the units place could be filled in five ways.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.100
Once the Units place is filled

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:59.300
the tens place would be filled with any of the remaining four digits .

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:01.600
And once two digits are utilized.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:06.540
The hundredths place can be filled with any one of the remaining three digits.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.920
Three times four times five, will also give us the same answer.

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:12.400
60 Ways.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:15.160
If you really understood this,

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:20.020
then understanding the second stated condition would be super easy.

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:23.020
Let's repeat the question on a new page.

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:28.100
This time we solve the question keeping in mind the second condition.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.380
Given these five digits.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:35.900
How many three-digit numbers can be formed assuming repetition is allowed?

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:42.340
So now we are allowed to consider numbers like 111 or 322 and so on.

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:45.740
So we have three slots for the three digits.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:49.260
How many three-digit numbers can be formed when repetitions

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.900
are allowed?

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.180
I want you to try this.

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:56.080
Remember, repetitions are allowed.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.080
So now we are allowed to consider all numbers,

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.580
which we had ignored earlier.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:05.180
We should have the possible numbers greater than 60.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:06.700
Try it !

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:19.080
Okay, as we saw earlier. Let's go slot by slot.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:22.500
In how many ways can the hundredths place be filled.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:25.900
It can be filled with any one of the five digits we have.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.780
It can be filled in five ways.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:32.080
Now in how many ways can the second slot be filled?

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:37.100
Think well, the second slot can also be filled in five ways.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:41.480
Why? It's because repetitions are allowed.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.500
If we used up one digit here,

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:46.500
The same one can be used here as well.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.860
So no matter what digit is used in the hundreds place

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:53.160
the tens place can be filled with any one of the five digits

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.920
we have been given.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.280
And similarly,

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:00.660
the third slot can also be filled with any one of the five digits.

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:02.500
Five ways again.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:05.340
If we have one in the hundreds place.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:08.060
The same one can be used in the tens place.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:10.340
And in the units place as well.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.760
There are no restrictions here.

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.140
So as we are filling in the first and the second and the third slot.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:23.660
We multiply these three numbers and get the answer as 125 ways.

00:08:23.860 --> 00:08:27.440
What does this answer imply relative to the previous one?

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.680
Let's go back and see the previous answer.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:32.940
If repetition wasn't allowed.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:37.240
There were 60 ways in which we can form three-digit numbers.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:42.440
And if repetition is allowed there are 125 ways.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.480
Why has the number increased?

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.340
It's obvious.

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:53.540
Here, apart from the no repetition ones like 123, 314, 245.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:55.320
We have allowed numbers like

00:08:55.480 --> 00:09:01.840
111, 222, 434 and many more like them to be considered.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:04.700
So I hope both cases are clear!

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.700
Repetition allowed, and not allowed.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.640
Which case do you think is easier to solve?

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.160
Think.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:14.800
It is the repetition allowed case.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:18.660
We don't have to worry about any of the conditions given.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:20.880
It makes life really easy,

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:27.020
and you will realize why when you watch the further sessions.

